/T (Explore additionally heuristic choises and routing with a board game \(optional\) After exploring the routing algorithm concepts through the physical activities in the schoolyard, you can optionally use the popular board game "Ticket to Ride" to organise a last playful session and explore the concepts more quitely. The closest games library near you will likely have several versions of it to lend to you. You can try to contextualise it as the map collection is wide so children can relate to something they know - You can find maps of Europe, France, Germany, the UK, Italy, and The Netherlands. )
/E (Explore additionally heuristic choises and routing with a board game \(optional\) After exploring the routing algorithm concepts through the physical activities in the schoolyard, you can optionally use the popular board game "Ticket to Ride" to organise a last playful session and explore the concepts more quitely. The closest games library near you will likely have several versions of it to lend to you. You can try to contextualise it as the map collection is wide so children can relate to something they know - You can find maps of Europe, France, Germany, the UK, Italy, and The Netherlands. )
