585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 89 0 R
/T (This creates a situation where some pupils \(nodes\) in the network might receive multiple balls \(packets\) simultaneously. When a pupil receives multiple balls at once, they must make a decision about which ball to pass first - this simulates how computer networks handle traffic congestion. Students can experiment with different strategies:)
/E (This creates a situation where some pupils \(nodes\) in the network might receive multiple balls \(packets\) simultaneously. When a pupil receives multiple balls at once, they must make a decision about which ball to pass first - this simulates how computer networks handle traffic congestion. Students can experiment with different strategies:)
/Pg 12 0 R
>>
endobj
